From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: social4hyq <social4hyq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 04 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] OHOS: download pnpm/bun from the @ohos-npm-ports ports.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

vp downloads a native package manager (pnpm >= 12, bun) from its npm
platform package, whose name is hard-coded per OS/arch. OHOS has no
official package, and the musl ones that the previous revision of this
patch borrowed do not work here: the bun binary needs a libstdc++ the
system does not have, and the pnpm binary is unsigned and takes its store
lock under the read-only /tmp. ohos-npm-ports republishes both as
signed, OHOS-built platform packages:

  @ohos-npm-ports/pnpm-exe.openharmony-arm64
  @ohos-npm-ports/oven-bun-openharmony-arm64

Port versions are `<upstream>-<revision>` (e.g. 12.8.1-2), so:

- the platform package name on ohos is the port, and its registry version
  is the highest published `<upstream>-<N>`; the <DATA>/package_manager
  cache directory keeps using the upstream version;
- `latest` and range resolution on ohos only consider versions a port
  exists for (pnpm < 12 is plain JS and needs no port), instead of
  resolving a version that would 404;
- nothing signs the binary at runtime any more (the former 0003 shelled
  out to selfsign), as the ports ship signed.

A `packageManager` hash still names the official pnpm main tarball and
is verified against it unchanged.
